  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "This team doesn't need to lead early to win close games.",
    "what_this_means": "Jackson Merrill's two-run homer in the second inning broke a tie and gave them air, but the real story was what happened after. The Giants scraped back to within one by the fourth, and the game stayed tight the rest of the way. Kyle Hart lasted three innings, which meant the bullpen had to hold a one-run lead for six innings. Morejon closed it out with three strikeouts in 1.1 innings, and nobody broke. This is a team that can win with pitching doing the heavy lifting and one offensive moment mattering enough. Three straight one-run wins. That math gets harder.",
